            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: what did nammakaṁ mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: పొలం",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పొలం (polaṁ) — \"a field\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పొలం (polaṁ) is a field under cultivation — not open ground, but somebody's, with a boundary and a name and a రైతు who walks it every morning."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The word is inherited. A గ్రామం is measured by its పొలం (polaṁ) far more than by its houses, and directions in the country are given by whose పొలం (polaṁ) you pass rather than by any బాట."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Going out to the పొలం (polaṁ) before ఉదయం and coming back after సాయంత్రం is the shape of the day the rest of this chapter describes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The ground everything else here stands on."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
