            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: what did polaṁ mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: వరి",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "వరి (vari) — \"paddy\", rice while it is still standing."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Telugu counts rice three times over and this is the first of them: వరి (vari) in the పొలం (polaṁ), బియ్యం once it is husked, అన్నం once it is cooked. Three words, three states, and none of them will stand in for another."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The word is inherited and it names the plant. English has one word for the lot and has to borrow \"paddy\" from Malay to get the same distinction; Telugu had it from the start."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A వరి (vari) పొలం (polaṁ) under water with the seedlings just pushed in is the picture the coast is built on, and what is being pushed in is the మొక్క from earlier in this book."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two: the ground and what is standing in it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
