        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: గడ్డి",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "గడ్డి (gaḍḍi) — \"grass\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "గడ్డి (gaḍḍi) is grass, and in a village it mostly means fodder — what gets cut at the edge of the పొలం (polaṁ) and carried back for the గేదె and the మేక."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The word is inherited. It covers straw as well, meaning what is left of the వరి (vari) once the grain is off, so one word runs all the way from the living plant to the dry stalk stacked beside the house."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "గడ్డి (gaḍḍi) does insulting work too. Calling something గడ్డి (gaḍḍi) is calling it worthless, which is what tends to happen to a word that means \"the part nobody eats\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three, and this is what the animals get."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
