        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: కల్లం",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కల్లం (kallaṁ) — \"a threshing floor\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కల్లం (kallaṁ) is the threshing floor: a flat patch of ground beaten hard and swept clean, where the cut వరి (vari) is separated from its గడ్డి (gaḍḍi)."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The word is inherited. A కల్లం (kallaṁ) belongs to the గ్రామం rather than to one house, and the order in which families take their turn on it is settled by custom rather than by asking — the kind of arrangement a village is full of."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It gets swept with a చీపురు before anything is laid down on it, and that sweeping is taken about as seriously as the ముగ్గు at a doorstep."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Four: where the year's work gets finished."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
