          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: పంట",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పంట (paṇṭa) — \"a harvest\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పంట (paṇṭa) is the harvest — the crop standing and the crop taken in, both at once. It is inherited, and it is what this whole chapter has been walking towards: పొలం (polaṁ), వరి (vari), గడ్డి (gaḍḍi), కల్లం (kallaṁ), and then పంట (paṇṭa)."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Telugu uses it well outside the field. A good year at anything is a మంచి పంట (paṇṭa), and somebody talking about how their children turned out will reach for the word without meaning anything about rice at all."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "When the పంట (paṇṭa) is in and the కల్లం (kallaṁ) is swept, the day and the season finish together, and there is nothing left to do but say వెళ్ళొస్తాను."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five: పొలం (polaṁ), వరి (vari), గడ్డి (gaḍḍi), కల్లం (kallaṁ), పంట (paṇṭa). A year's work in five words, and a good place to take your leave."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
